{"cases":[{"attack":true,"case":"The specification claims that the full audit log ensures complete reproducibility, but in parallel fetch scenarios the ordering of log entries may be non-deterministic due to race conditions. The mechanism does not provide a deterministic serialization strategy for concurrent fetches, so the log itself may not be reproducible, violating the requirement for a typed auditable terminal state.","target":"69c7c7d23b10eed6255f4732c4aca05e7c2817ea88ecb7703157bb5e4d85a9dc"},{"attack":true,"case":"The mechanism uses estimated_bytes for the pre-fetch budget check, while the terminal state records bytes_used. The exhaustion decision is based on an unrecorded estimate, not on actual bytes consumed. This makes the terminal state non-auditable with respect to the true exhaustion condition, and if the estimation method is non-deterministic or unspecified, the point of exhaustion is not reproducible.","target":"b15de5d9228f301afa37c930b214c6579e90eff0e93d125cfe91a54858ecb58e"}]}